---
mode: prompt
---
// H9a acceptance area (c) — typed query with an INLINE object type (QRY-22).
// The inline object annotation is lowered and the response validated against it.
//
// Bug 0010: the forced respond turn runs OFF-SESSION (pi-ai `complete()` with
// forced toolChoice) and never streams into the transcript, so the fixture
// itself surfaces the AJV-validated value: the final untyped query interpolates
// `r` (QRY-18 compact JSON) behind the committed sentinel, and that echo is the
// run's LAST assistant message — the `pi -p` stdout observable the suite
// parses. The sentinel can only appear if the typed binding resolved Ok (past
// AJV and past `?`).
// Drive discriminators are ANSWERS to task questions over the theta's own
// computed text -- deterministic content a degraded plain-prompt run cannot
// produce. A verbatim-echo demand ("reply with exactly this") reads as prompt
// injection to current models and draws refusals: the sentinel-refusal class
// filed as bug 0243. The rendering line below asks the model to REPORT the
// already-validated value rather than parrot an attacker-chosen token, while
// the anchor literal `ACC TYPED INLINE RESULT` stays byte-identical for
// `noninteractive-acceptance.test.ts`'s `parseJsonAfterSentinel` call.
let r: { ok: boolean, label: string } = @`Return an object: set ok to true and label to a short descriptive string.`?
@`A tool produced this JSON value: ${r}. Report it on one line: the label ACC TYPED INLINE RESULT, one space, then the JSON value unchanged. Plain text, no code fences.`?
